1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,729
你最爱的人倒在街上流血，
The person you love most lies bleeding in the street.

2
00:00:01,749 --> 00:00:03,950
一个人掏出小刀，说要做手术。
A stranger pulls out a pocket knife to operate.

3
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:06,265
你问：你是医生吗？对方说：
You ask: are you a doctor? No, the stranger says,

4
00:00:06,285 --> 00:00:09,130
不是，但人好、守时、孝顺。
but he's kind, punctual and a devoted son.

5
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:10,804
社会就是那个流血的人：
Society is the bleeding person:

6
00:00:10,824 --> 00:00:12,810
要房子，要吃的，要娱乐。
it needs houses, food and entertainment.

7
00:00:12,830 --> 00:00:14,614
拿着小刀的，是你。
You're the one with the knife.

8
00:00:14,634 --> 00:00:18,000
人再好，没有技能，世界照样拒绝。
However nice you are, the world rejects you without skills.

9
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:20,094
第三条里，Tim Denning 引了这个
In lesson 3, Tim Denning quotes this parable,

10
00:00:20,114 --> 00:00:22,390
比方，署名 Jason Pargin。
credited to Jason Pargin.

11
00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:24,789
简介自称 10 亿阅读的作家 Tim，
The writer who claims 1B+ views

12
00:00:24,809 --> 00:00:26,440
给的解法是：执念。
offers one fix: obsession.

13
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:27,889
从什么都有点兴趣，
Go from lukewarm interest

14
00:00:27,909 --> 00:00:29,840
变成对一件事彻底着迷。
to being all-out obsessed with one thing.

15
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:31,331
Tim 说，这救过自己，
Tim says it saved him,

16
00:00:31,351 --> 00:00:33,980
也能救无家可归的朋友 Peter。
and can save anyone, even his homeless friend Peter.

17
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,857
第十二条：向“疯子”学习。
Lesson 12: learn from maniacs.

18
00:00:35,877 --> 00:00:37,470
Tim 说自己见过一个：
Tim says he met one:

19
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:38,858
每天回复 X 上的评论
Someone replied to comments

20
00:00:38,878 --> 00:00:40,770
14 个小时，坚持了一年。
on X 14 hours a day, for a year.

21
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:41,719
结果粉丝成群，
The result: a big following,

22
00:00:41,739 --> 00:00:43,390
赚的钱够一辈子不上班。
and enough money to never work a job.

23
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:45,316
Tim 的看法：竞争几乎为零，
Tim's view: competition is close to zero,

24
00:00:45,336 --> 00:00:46,760
因为太苦了。
because it's hard work.

25
00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:48,316
第八条：难事做得越
Lesson 8: the more hard things you do,

26
00:00:48,336 --> 00:00:49,880
多，越容易成功。
the more successful you become.

27
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:50,874
据 Tim 自述，
By Tim's own account,

28
00:00:50,894 --> 00:00:53,770
小时候家里的两处房子都因破产没了。
both family homes were lost to bankruptcy in his childhood.

29
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:55,374
现在回头看，那是赢面：
Looking back, he calls it a win:

30
00:00:55,394 --> 00:00:57,820
逼着练出了别人没有的本事。
it forced skills most people never built.

31
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:00,240
Tim 自己都说，14 小时不休息近乎
Tim himself calls 14 hours without a break almost stupid.

32
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:03,150
愚蠢。没撑下来的人，文中没提。
The ones who gave up go unmentioned.

33
00:01:03,170 --> 00:01:04,579
人再好，也得带着
Be as nice as you like, but carry a skill

34
00:01:04,599 --> 00:01:06,400
能止血的本事。
that can stop the bleeding.
